5.2 VCSEL Reliability

850 nm VCSELs have field experience of over 100 million units with random failure rate lower than 1 FIT . Internal random failure rate tests accumulated ~0.3 billion device hours, showing < 1 FIT at 40°C and < 7 FIT at 105°C . Wear-out lifetime exceeds 10 years at 70°C/8 mA operation . These are random failure rates (FIT), distinct from wear-out lifetime (TT1%F). The specific 30 FIT figure is from particular accelerated-aging populations and is labelled as such.

5.3 Polymer Waveguide Reliability

Flexible polymer waveguides exhibit stability in damp heat (2000 h in 85°C/85% RH) and thermal shock (500 cycles from −40° to +120°C), with optical loss less than 0.05 dB/cm at 850 nm . These are material- and process-specific results, treated as hypotheses pending measurement on the exact film used in the robot demonstrator.

5.4 CWDM vs. DWDM Power

CWDM systems deploy uncooled DFB lasers and wideband optical filters, providing lower power dissipation, smaller size, and less cost . A CWDM transmitter consumes approximately 0.5 W, while a DWDM transmitter with TEC consumes approximately 4 W per channel. The energy per bit is:

E_{\text{bit}} = \frac{P_{\text{laser}} + P_{\text{TEC}} + P_{\text{driver}} + P_{\text{tuning}}}{B}

CWDM+SDM superiority remains a hypothesis to be tested.

