Appendix C: Functional Safety Calculation Templates

C.1 FMEDA Template

For each component i participating in a safety function S, the FMEDA records:

Parameter Symbol Formula
Total failure rate \lambda_i From database or field data
Safe detected rate \lambda_{SD,i} \lambda_i \cdot \text{DC}_{\text{safe}}
Safe undetected rate \lambda_{SU,i} \lambda_i \cdot (1 - \text{DC}_{\text{safe}})
Dangerous detected rate \lambda_{DD,i} \lambda_i \cdot \text{DC}_{\text{dangerous}}
Dangerous undetected rate \lambda_{DU,i} \lambda_i \cdot (1 - \text{DC}_{\text{dangerous}})

The diagnostic coverage is defined as:

DC_{\text{safe}} = \frac{\lambda_{SD}}{\lambda_{SD} + \lambda_{SU}}

DC_{\text{dangerous}} = \frac{\lambda_{DD}}{\lambda_{DD} + \lambda_{DU}}

The Safe Failure Fraction is:

\text{SFF} = \frac{\sum \lambda_{SD} + \sum \lambda_{SU} + \sum \lambda_{DD}}{\sum \lambda_{SD} + \sum \lambda_{SU} + \sum \lambda_{DD} + \sum \lambda_{DU}}

C.2 SFF/HFT Tables (Route 1H)

Type A Components:

SFF HFT = 0 HFT = 1 HFT = 2
< 60% SIL 1 SIL 2 SIL 2
60%–90% SIL 2 SIL 3 SIL 3
90%–99% SIL 3 SIL 4 SIL 4
≥ 99% SIL 3 SIL 4 SIL 4

Type B Components:

SFF HFT = 0 HFT = 1 HFT = 2
< 60% Not allowed SIL 1 SIL 2
60%–90% SIL 1 SIL 2 SIL 3
90%–99% SIL 2 SIL 3 SIL 4
≥ 99% SIL 3 SIL 4 SIL 4

Type A components are simple components with well-defined failure modes and completely determined behaviour under fault conditions. Type B components are all components where these characteristics do not apply, including components containing software. For photonic elements: VCSELs, detectors, and polymer connectors are classified as Type B; passive optical components may qualify as Type A if failure modes are fully characterised.

C.3 PFH Calculation for Series Architecture

For a series reliability structure with independent failures:

\text{PFH}_S = \sum_{i=1}^{n} \text{PFH}_i

with \text{PFH}_i = \lambda_{DU,i} for high-demand mode. This is valid only when all subsystems must function and failures are independent. For redundant architectures, the simple sum is replaced by the appropriate KooN formula with common-cause correction.

C.4 Common-Cause Failure: Beta-Factor Model

The \beta-factor model splits the failure rate into independent and common-cause components:

\lambda_{\text{CCF}} = \beta \cdot \lambda

\lambda_{\text{IND}} = (1 - \beta) \cdot \lambda

For a switching fabric with M elements, the independent contribution to PFH is (1-\beta) \lambda_{\text{switch}}, and the common-cause contribution is \beta \lambda_{\text{switch}} affecting all elements simultaneously.

C.5 Residual Error Budget: Numerical Allocation

For SIL 3, the total PFH ceiling is 10^{-7}/h. IEC 61784-3 recommends that communication contribute less than 1% of this budget, yielding \text{RER}_{\text{SCL}} \leq 10^{-9}/h.

