Appendix D: IEC 61784-3 Residual Error Model — Complete Formulation

D.1 Black Channel Principle

The black channel principle assumes that the transmission channel is not trusted and that all safety measures are implemented in the Safety Communication Layer (SCL). The residual error rate for the SCL is decomposed into contributions from authenticity, timeliness, masquerade, and data integrity errors.

D.2 Authenticity Residual Error Rate

For connection-IDs transmitted as Authentication-Code (A-code) with every package, and the rate of mistrusted messages not exceeding the message rate \nu:

RR_A = 0

D.3 Timeliness Residual Error Rate

RR_T = 2^{-LT} \cdot w \cdot R_T \cdot RP_{\text{FSCP\_T}}

where LT is the bitlength of the Timeliness-Code (T-code), w is the number of accepted T-codes, R_T is the rate of not-actual messages (worst case \nu), and RP_{\text{FSCP\_T}} is the residual error probability of timeliness measures.

D.4 Masquerade Residual Error Rate

RR_M = 2^{-LA} \cdot 2^{-LT} \cdot w \cdot 2^{-r} \cdot RP_u \cdot 2^{-LR} \cdot R_M

where LA is the bitlength of the A-code, LT is the bitlength of the T-code, r is the CRC signature length, RP_u is the residual error probability for other data fields, LR is the bitlength of the redundant message part, and R_M is the masquerade rate.

D.5 Data Integrity Residual Error Rate

For CRC-based integrity with a comprehensive channel model, the residual error probability is a function of the bit error rate, the SPDU length, and the CRC signature length. For a bit error rate of 10^{-2} and a CRC signature of length r, the residual error probability is approximately:

\text{REP}_{\text{CRC}} \approx 2^{-r} \cdot f(\text{BER}, L_{\text{SPDU}})

The FSoE specification adopts \text{BER} = 10^{-2} as the worst-case channel condition, resulting in no restrictions on device manufacturers and end users when appropriate CRC lengths are used.

D.6 Total Residual Error Rate

\lambda_{SC} = RR_A + RR_T + RR_M + \text{REP}_{\text{CRC}}

For a SIL 3 application with less than 10^{-7}/h dangerous failures for the entire safety function, the target is \lambda_{SC} \leq 10^{-9}/h.

