Appendix E: Crosstalk Penalty Derivation

E.1 Homodyne Crosstalk: Physical Origin

Homodyne crosstalk arises in OADMs between the signal added at the add port and the residual of the signal dropped at the same wavelength. The interfering field beats with the signal field in the photodetector, producing signal-crosstalk beat noise. The power penalty is defined as the increase in received optical power required to maintain the same SNR (or Q-factor) for a given BER.

E.2 Amplitude-Beating Derivation

The received optical power in the presence of homodyne crosstalk is:

P_{\text{rec}}(X) = \frac{Q \cdot \sigma_r + Q^2 \cdot q \Delta f}{R \cdot (1 - X \cdot Q^2)}

where X is the crosstalk level, \sigma_r is the receiver noise, q is the electron charge, \Delta f is the receiver bandwidth, and R is the responsivity. The power penalty is:

\text{PP} = 10 \log\left(\frac{P_{\text{rec}}(X)}{P_{\text{rec}}(0)}\right) = -10 \log(1 - X \cdot Q^2)

For a BER of 10^{-9}, Q = 6. This formulation assumes worst-case polarization alignment of the interfering signal and an optimized decision threshold.

E.3 Generalised Form with Extinction Ratio

Including the signal extinction ratio r:

\text{PP}_{\text{homodyne}} \approx -10 \log_{10}\left(1 - 4 \epsilon Q^2 \frac{1+r}{(1-r)^2}\right)

For ideal extinction (r \to 0):

\text{PP}_{\text{homodyne}} \approx -10 \log_{10}(1 - 4 \epsilon Q^2)

The critical crosstalk at which the penalty diverges is \epsilon_{\text{crit}} = 1/(4Q^2) \approx -21.6 dB for Q = 6.

E.4 Coherent Accumulation: Deterministic and Statistical Limits

For N cascaded OADMs with worst-case coherent phase alignment:

\epsilon_{\text{cum}} = \left(\sum_{i=1}^{N} \sqrt{\epsilon_i}\right)^2 = N^2 \epsilon_{\text{stage}}

With \epsilon_{\text{stage}} = 10^{-3} (-30 dB) and \text{PP}_{\max} = 1 dB:

1 - 4 \epsilon_{\text{cum}} Q^2 \geq 10^{-0.1} \approx 0.794

\epsilon_{\text{cum}} \leq \frac{1 - 0.794}{4 \times 36} \approx 1.43 \times 10^{-3}

N_{\max} \approx \sqrt{1.43} \approx 1.2

For statistical phase averaging, the accumulation is incoherent:

\epsilon_{\text{cum}} \approx N \cdot \epsilon_{\text{stage}}

yielding N_{\max} \approx 1.43 under the same penalty constraint. Literature reports 1 dB OSNR penalty after 13–24 cascaded OADMs for NRZ and Nyquist-shaped signals, assuming statistical phase averaging and polarization scrambling, which are not applicable to worst-case safety-critical channels.

E.5 Sensitivity Analysis

Per-stage isolation N_{\max} (worst-case coherent) N_{\max} (statistical)
-30 dB 1.2 1.4
-35 dB 3.8 4.5
-40 dB 12.0 14.3

With a 0.5 dB statistical margin, N_{\max} \approx 1.7 for -30 dB per stage.

