Appendix I: Measurement Protocols

I.1 H_A Measurement Protocol

Objective: Demonstrate > 30% mass/volume reduction at equal SIL 3 compliance versus copper.

Apparatus:

· Same 6-DOF arm for both copper and photonic configurations
· Calibrated scale with ±0.1 g resolution
· Water displacement or 3D scanning for volume measurement

Procedure:

1. Weigh and measure the copper cable harness.
2. Replace with photonic hybrid harness.
3. Weigh and measure the photonic harness.
4. Run the identical T1–T5 workload suite on both configurations.
5. Demonstrate SIL 3 compliance via identical black-channel safety protocol in both arms.

Output: Mass and volume reduction percentages, with confidence intervals.

I.2 H_B Measurement Protocol

Objective: Demonstrate lower lifecycle cost for CWDM+SDM over POF/polymer versus DWDM-on-silicon.

Procedure:

1. Measure energy per bit for both configurations under T1–T5.
2. Measure PER under T5 vibration/thermal exposure.
3. Measure system-level reconfiguration latency for keyframe transitions.
4. Perform Monte Carlo lifecycle cost simulation with \geq 10^4 samples.
5. Use connector replacement interval from drag-chain cycle testing.

Output: Pareto front in (E_{\text{bit}}, \text{PER}, \tau_{\text{reconfig}}, C_{\text{lifecycle}}) space.

